4,1,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,We need a structure that ensures financial stability without creating barriers for new members. I suggest we examine the last year's ledger of outgoings and the sign-up records for mid-year joiners to understand our costs and growth.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Those are sensible starting points, Asuka. However, we should also consider the human cost of our administration. I'm curious about the outgoing treasurer's logged hours and the tally of the sign-in sheets to gauge the actual workload.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Benjamin. To ensure fairness, I think we should also look at the rota against the attendance record and the weekday turnout since the summer outings to see how members actually utilize the club.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Financials and hours are all well and good, but let's not forget the people. I'll look into the weekday turnout since the summer outings and the quieter members at the winter social. We need to see who's actually engaged.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Takumi,,We can't just guess the numbers like we did last time. We need to know exactly what's coming in. I'll check the bank statements on last year's renewals and the last year's ledger of outgoings.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"It seems we are all in agreement that financial data and attendance are key. However, we must be careful not to over-analyze individual behavior. I still believe the mid-year joiner records are essential for maintaining accessibility.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Accessibility is a noble goal, Asuka, but let's not forget that a system that is too ""accessible"" often becomes a nightmare for the person managing the ledger. Simplicity is a kindness to our future treasurer.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Simplicity is important, but so is equity. If a small group is doing all the work while others rarely attend, a simple flat fee might feel unfair to those most invested in the club.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, ""equity"" is a heavy word for a social club. If people are hesitating to show up, a complex ""fair"" fee might just be another excuse for them to stay home. Let's keep it rational.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, being rational means having real numbers, not just feelings. If we don't know the actual balance and the cost of running things, any fee we set is just a gamble. We need stability first.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"Stability is necessary, but not at the cost of inclusivity. If we make the fee too rigid or the process too transparent, we risk alienating those who prefer to blend in. We must balance the books without scrutinizing members.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, while I appreciate the desire for discretion, we must avoid creating a system that is so opaque it becomes an administrative labyrinth. A bit of transparency usually saves the treasurer from endless queries.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,Perhaps we can find a middle ground. Transparency doesn't have to mean scrutiny; it can simply mean a structure that reflects the reality of our usage. I still believe understanding the attendance patterns is vital for a fair decision.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, you're still obsessed with ""fairness."" The real issue is whether people feel like they belong enough to just show up. Let's see if the data actually shows a decline in commitment.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, commitment doesn't pay the bills. If we don't have a predictable income, the club fails regardless of how people ""feel."" We need a structure based on hard facts, not hopes.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"We have a clear divide between financial pragmatism and member experience. To move forward, I will look into the last year's ledger of outgoings and the sign-up records for mid-year joiners.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall stick with my original suggestions. I will examine the outgoing treasurer's logged hours and the tally of the sign-in sheets. Let us see if the administrative burden is as heavy as I suspect.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will look into the rota against the attendance record and the weekday turnout since the summer outings. I want to see if the burden of effort is shared equally among us.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll stick to my plan. I'm looking into the weekday turnout since the summer outings and the quieter members at the winter social. Let's see if the ""commitment"" is actually slipping.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm sticking to my guns. I'll check the bank statements on last year's renewals and the last year's ledger of outgoings. I won't let us walk into next year blindly.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
