30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The ledger shows that seventy percent of our costs are fixed overheads like hall hire and insurance. Additionally, mid-year joiners require manual calculations, which suggests our current process for newcomers is inefficient and potentially discouraging.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears my suspicions were correct. The treasurer's logs reveal that chasing session-by-session payments is a grueling task, consuming six times the effort of a yearly collection. We are essentially paying for ""flexibility"" with someone's sanity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are concerning. The same nine people are handling almost all the setup and locking up, and they are also our most frequent attendees. It seems a small core is carrying the entire club.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's exactly as I suspected. The moment we introduced door charges for the outings, the weekday turnout dropped by a third. People stopped feeling like the club was theirs; they started weighing the cost.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, that's exactly why we can't guess. The bank statements show people struggle to pay upfront, yet 70% of our costs are fixed. We're bleeding money on overheads while chasing payments. We need a guaranteed floor.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, a guaranteed floor is necessary, but we must be careful. @Shunichi's point about the turnout drop proves that when costs become too visible or transactional, people withdraw. We need a system that covers overheads without feeling like a barrier.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, while I agree that psychological barriers matter, we cannot ignore the administrative toll. If we opt for a ""low-barrier"" transactional system, we are simply volunteering the next treasurer for a part-time job they didn't sign up for.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I understand the burden, but we must also address the imbalance of effort. If the same few people are doing all the work and attending most often, a flat fee feels like a subsidy for the inactive.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, you're still treating this like a business transaction. If we penalize the inactive or reward the ""core,"" we just solidify the divide. We need to make coming here a habit again, not a calculation.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, it's not about subsidies, it's about survival. If we don't cover those fixed costs, there is no club for anyone to attend. We need a structure that secures the money first.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, survival is the goal, but not at the cost of the club's soul. If we make the fee too rigid, we lose the newcomers who keep us fresh. We need a way to cover overheads discreetly.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, ""discreetly"" is often a synonym for ""administratively complex."" If we try to hide the costs through a convoluted system, we are merely shifting the burden from the member's wallet to the treasurer's evening. Logic dictates we prioritize simplicity.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, simplicity is a virtue, but not if it ignores the resentment building among those who do the heavy lifting. If we don't acknowledge the disparity in contribution, we risk losing the very core that keeps us running.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, resentment is a choice. If you focus on who's ""carrying"" the club, you're just building a wall. We need to stop making members calculate the value of their attendance before they even leave the house.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, you're talking about walls, but the biggest wall is a bankrupt account. If we don't have a predictable income to cover that 70% fixed cost, the club closes. That's the only calculation that actually matters.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We are circling the same points. We need a solution that covers the fixed costs and reduces the treasurer's workload, but does so without making membership feel like a transaction or a surveillance exercise. Let's see the options.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. We have established that we need a balance between financial viability and administrative sanity. I look forward to seeing which of the options manages to be both fiscally responsible and merciful to the treasurer.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I hope the options provide a way to recognize the commitment of our core members without creating the transactional barriers @Shunichi is worried about. Fairness and sustainability must go hand in hand.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's just hope the options aren't as rigid as Takumi's mindset. If we treat this like a corporate audit, we'll have a perfectly balanced ledger and a completely empty room. Let's see the proposals.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, call it what you want, but a ""corporate audit"" is better than a bankrupt club. I'm not being rigid; I'm being realistic. Let's see the options and pick the one that actually secures our future.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
